    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0666" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg542"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/103</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 10.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4130</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s telegram, No.
                    9 of January 7, 5 p.m., concerning the Chinese Arms Embargo, and as stated in my
                    telegram of today’s date,<anchor n="45" xml:id="d494-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    enclose a copy of a Note from the Foreign Office dated the 22nd instant,
                    received on the 24th, in reply to the Embassy’s Memorandum of the 10th
                        instant,<anchor n="45" xml:id="d494-f2"/> which was based upon the
                    Department’s telegraphic instructions. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Butler
                            Wright</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>


                <xi:include href="d494-a1.xml" xpointer="d494-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
